@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+# OWNER APPROVAL — R0039 / #215 — Prospective Package Capacity Amendment
+
+I approve a prospective increase of the canonical plugin and standalone compatibility compressed-package limits from **327,680 bytes (320 KiB) to 393,216 bytes (384 KiB) per artifact**, retaining the mandatory **2,000-byte reserve**.
+
+This is a deliberate owner decision following the measured R0039 package-capacity investigation. The objective is to permit complete, readable, secure and functional implementations without forcing disproportionate source compression or representation changes.
+
+I authorise the entitled package-contract/shared integration owner to implement this narrow prospective amendment, including the versioned budget declaration, necessary coordinated validation and installer checks, and exact-source evidence.
+
+Preserve the original historical budget and its evidence. Verify that no external host or distribution limit prohibits the revised budget. Do not weaken membership, integrity, security, installation, rollback, source-currentness or runtime acceptance controls. No pre-existing failing result becomes a historical PASS through this amendment.
+
+Defer discretionary final package-size optimisation until the currently commissioned source implementations have been integrated and the complete shipping population is measurable. Perform that reassessment before final combined package acceptance, release or any issue closure that depends on it.
+
+Do not repeat the completed compression investigation merely to justify this approved budget change.
+
+R0039's separate LR10-C writer-provenance problem, native acceptance, shared-owner integration and other outstanding requirements remain fully applicable.
+
+No merge, issue closure, release or protected campaign mutation is authorised here. Return the implemented exact-source change and its affected verification through the existing owner/conductor route.
+
+
+
+One caution we have discovered about R0039: Raising the cap resolves only the capacity obstacle after the owner implements and verifies the amendment. Its unexplained historical `.controller` writer event remains open. I am deferring another engineering commission on that until the relevant filesystem/runner owner can supply writer provenance or a reliably reproducing case.
